{
 "1": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 330\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Histogram with frequency polygon, and less-than ogive with the median read at cumulative frequency 12.5\">\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"200\" y=\"30\">Histogram + frequency polygon</text><text x=\"555\" y=\"30\">Less-than ogive</text></g>\n          <g style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"170\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"70\"/></g>\n          <g style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.5\"><rect x=\"95\" y=\"250\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\"/><rect x=\"130\" y=\"210\" width=\"35\" height=\"60\"/><rect x=\"165\" y=\"150\" width=\"35\" height=\"120\"/><rect x=\"200\" y=\"90\" width=\"35\" height=\"180\"/><rect x=\"235\" y=\"190\" width=\"35\" height=\"80\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"230\" width=\"35\" height=\"40\"/></g>\n          <polyline points=\"77.5,270 112.5,250 147.5,210 182.5,150 217.5,90 252.5,190 287.5,230 322.5,270\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M109,250a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M144,210a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M179,150a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M214,90a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M249,190a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M284,230a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M60,60 V270 H340 M420,60 V270 H700\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"95\" y=\"288\">30</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"288\">40</text><text x=\"165\" y=\"288\">50</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\">60</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"288\">70</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"288\">80</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"288\">90</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"314\">Marks (class boundaries)</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"288\">30</text><text x=\"465\" y=\"288\">40</text><text x=\"510\" y=\"288\">50</text><text x=\"555\" y=\"288\">60</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"288\">70</text><text x=\"645\" y=\"288\">80</text><text x=\"690\" y=\"288\">90</text><text x=\"560\" y=\"314\">Marks (upper class boundary)</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\"><text x=\"52\" y=\"274\">0</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"174\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"74\">10</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"274\">0</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"194\">10</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"114\">20</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"74\">25</text></g>\n          <text transform=\"translate(26,170) rotate(-90)\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Frequency</text>\n          <text transform=\"translate(380,170) rotate(-90)\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cumulative frequency</text>\n          <polyline points=\"420,270 465,262 510,238 555,190 600,118 645,86 690,70\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M416.5,270a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M461.5,262a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M506.5,238a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M551.5,190a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M596.5,118a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M641.5,86a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0 M686.5,70a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 7,0a3.5,3.5 0 1 0 -7,0\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M420,170 H567.5 V270\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\"><text x=\"428\" y=\"162\">n/2 = 12.5</text><text x=\"575\" y=\"250\">median ≈ 62.8</text><text x=\"232\" y=\"84\">peak 60–70</text></g>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.1.1</b> The 25 test marks of the worked example. Left: the histogram (bars touch) with the frequency polygon drawn through the class midpoints and closed at 25 and 95. Right: the less-than ogive, plotted at upper class boundaries; the dashed line goes across from n/2 = 12.5 and down to the median, about 62.8 marks.</figcaption>\n      </figure>",
 "2": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 320\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Dot plot of 11 delivery times with mode, median, mean, interquartile range, upper fence and the outlier 59 marked\">\n          <text x=\"360\" y=\"28\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">11 delivery times (minutes): centre and spread</text>\n          <path d=\"M218,112 V196 M190,86 V196 M260,138 V196\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"190\" y=\"80\">mode 25</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"106\">median 27</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"132\">mean 30</text></g>\n          <path d=\"M50,210 H680 M50,210 v6 M120,210 v6 M190,210 v6 M260,210 v6 M330,210 v6 M400,210 v6 M470,210 v6 M540,210 v6 M610,210 v6 M680,210 v6\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"50\" y=\"232\">15</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"232\">20</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"232\">25</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"232\">30</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"232\">35</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"232\">40</text><text x=\"470\" y=\"232\">45</text><text x=\"540\" y=\"232\">50</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"232\">55</text><text x=\"680\" y=\"232\">60</text></g>\n          <path d=\"M86,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M142,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M170,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M184,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M184,186a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M212,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M240,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M268,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M310,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0 M338,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M660,200a6,6 0 1 0 12,0a6,6 0 1 0 -12,0\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n          <text x=\"666\" y=\"178\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">outlier 59</text>\n          <path d=\"M526,96 V204\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n          <text x=\"534\" y=\"110\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\">upper fence</text><text x=\"534\" y=\"128\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\">34 + 1.5 × 10 = 49</text>\n          <path d=\"M176,246 v10 H316 v-10\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"/>\n          <text x=\"326\" y=\"258\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\">IQR: Q1 = 24 to Q3 = 34, so IQR = 10</text>\n          <path d=\"M106.7,278 v10 H413.3 v-10\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"/>\n          <text x=\"423\" y=\"290\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\">x̄ ± s = 19.1 to 41.0</text>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.2.1</b> The worked example's data as a dot plot. The single 59 drags the mean (30) to the right of the median (27) and the mode (25), and stretches the standard deviation band; the IQR box of the middle half (24 to 34) ignores it. The dashed upper fence at 49 flags 59 as an outlier.</figcaption>\n      </figure>",
 "3": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 372\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Normal curve with mean 62 and standard deviation 8, right tail above 74 shaded, and brackets for the 68, 95 and 99.7 percent ranges\">\n          <defs><marker id=\"m33a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/></marker></defs>\n          <path d=\"M472,240 L472.0,175.1 L480.8,184.4 L489.6,192.9 L498.4,200.4 L507.2,207.1 L516.0,212.9 L524.8,217.9 L533.6,222.2 L542.4,225.8 L551.2,228.8 L560.0,231.2 L568.8,233.2 L577.6,234.8 L586.4,236.0 L595.2,237.0 L604.0,237.8 L612.8,238.4 L621.6,238.8 L630.4,239.1 L639.2,239.4 L639.2,240 Z\" style=\"fill:var(--live);fill-opacity:.4\"/>\n          <path d=\"M40.8,239.4 L49.6,239.1 L58.4,238.8 L67.2,238.4 L76.0,237.8 L84.8,237.0 L93.6,236.0 L102.4,234.8 L111.2,233.2 L120.0,231.2 L128.8,228.8 L137.6,225.8 L146.4,222.2 L155.2,217.9 L164.0,212.9 L172.8,207.1 L181.6,200.4 L190.4,192.9 L199.2,184.4 L208.0,175.1 L216.8,164.9 L225.6,154.1 L234.4,142.6 L243.2,130.8 L252.0,118.7 L260.8,106.6 L269.6,94.8 L278.4,83.5 L287.2,72.9 L296.0,63.5 L304.8,55.4 L313.6,48.8 L322.4,44.0 L331.2,41.0 L340.0,40.0 L348.8,41.0 L357.6,44.0 L366.4,48.8 L375.2,55.4 L384.0,63.5 L392.8,72.9 L401.6,83.5 L410.4,94.8 L419.2,106.6 L428.0,118.7 L436.8,130.8 L445.6,142.6 L454.4,154.1 L463.2,164.9 L472.0,175.1 L480.8,184.4 L489.6,192.9 L498.4,200.4 L507.2,207.1 L516.0,212.9 L524.8,217.9 L533.6,222.2 L542.4,225.8 L551.2,228.8 L560.0,231.2 L568.8,233.2 L577.6,234.8 L586.4,236.0 L595.2,237.0 L604.0,237.8 L612.8,238.4 L621.6,238.8 L630.4,239.1 L639.2,239.4\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M30,240 H650 M76,240 v6 M164,240 v6 M252,240 v6 M340,240 v6 M428,240 v6 M516,240 v6 M604,240 v6\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M340,40 V240\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n          <line x1=\"342\" y1=\"118.7\" x2=\"426\" y2=\"118.7\" style=\"stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\" marker-start=\"url(#m33a)\" marker-end=\"url(#m33a)\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"340\" y=\"30\">μ = 62</text><text x=\"384\" y=\"110\">σ = 8</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"262\">38</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"262\">46</text><text x=\"252\" y=\"262\">54</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"262\">62</text><text x=\"428\" y=\"262\">70</text><text x=\"516\" y=\"262\">78</text><text x=\"604\" y=\"262\">86</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"282\">−3</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"282\">−2</text><text x=\"252\" y=\"282\">−1</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"282\">0</text><text x=\"428\" y=\"282\">1</text><text x=\"516\" y=\"282\">2</text><text x=\"604\" y=\"282\">3</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\"><text x=\"662\" y=\"262\">marks</text><text x=\"662\" y=\"282\">z</text><text x=\"492\" y=\"152\">above 74 (z = 1.5):</text><text x=\"492\" y=\"170\">1 − 0.9332 = 6.68%</text></g>\n          <path d=\"M252,297 v8 H428 v-8 M164,322 v8 H516 v-8 M76,347 v8 H604 v-8\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"340\" y=\"301\">68.27% in 54 to 70</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"326\">95.45% in 46 to 78</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"351\">99.73% in 38 to 86</text></g>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.3.1</b> Marks ~ N(62, 8²) from the worked example, with the marks scale and the z scale under the same axis. The shaded right tail is the 6.68% who score above 74. The brackets show the empirical rule: each extra σ on both sides adds less area, because the tails are thin.</figcaption>\n      </figure>",
 "4": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 252\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four scatter plots with correlation 0.96, 0.02, minus 0.97 and 0.00 for a U-shaped pattern\">\n          <path d=\"M30,45 V195 H165 M210,45 V195 H345 M390,45 V195 H525 M570,45 V195 H702\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M38.5,167.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M51,171.2a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M63.5,137.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M76,152.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M88.5,123.8a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M101,103.8a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M113.5,111.2a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M126,85a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M138.5,91.2a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M151,57.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M218.5,115a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M231,152.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M243.5,90a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M256,165a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M268.5,102.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M281,140a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M293.5,77.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M306,127.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M318.5,152.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M331,115a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M398.5,72.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M411,66.2a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M423.5,95a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M436,88.8a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M448.5,125a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M461,121.2a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M473.5,152.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M486,143.8a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M498.5,162.5a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M511,183.8a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M578.5,62.4a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M591,107.9a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M603.5,142a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M616,164.7a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M628.5,176.1a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M641,176.1a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M653.5,164.7a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M666,142a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M678.5,107.9a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M691,62.4a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"220\">r = 0.96</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"220\">r = 0.02</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"220\">r = −0.97</text><text x=\"638\" y=\"220\">r = 0.00</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"240\">strong positive</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"240\">no linear link</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"240\">strong negative</text><text x=\"638\" y=\"240\">U-shape r misses</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"32\">A</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"32\">B</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"32\">C</text><text x=\"638\" y=\"32\">D</text></g>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.4.1</b> Four sets of ten points, with r computed from the plotted values. A and C hug a straight line, so |r| is near 1. B has no pattern. D has a perfect pattern, y = (x − 5.5)² scaled, yet r = 0, because its left half falls exactly as its right half rises. Correlation sees only straight lines.</figcaption>\n      </figure>",
 "5": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 322\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"EDA decision map from variable type to univariate and bivariate summaries and plots\">\n          <defs><marker id=\"m35a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/></marker></defs>\n          <g style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"150\" y=\"14\" width=\"420\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"84\" width=\"272\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"294\" y=\"84\" width=\"412\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/></g>\n          <g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.5\"><rect x=\"14\" y=\"146\" width=\"132\" height=\"92\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"154\" y=\"146\" width=\"132\" height=\"92\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"294\" y=\"146\" width=\"132\" height=\"92\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"434\" y=\"146\" width=\"132\" height=\"92\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"574\" y=\"146\" width=\"132\" height=\"92\" rx=\"8\"/></g>\n          <rect x=\"14\" y=\"266\" width=\"692\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n          <g style=\"stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\" marker-end=\"url(#m35a)\"><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"82\"/><line x1=\"420\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"82\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"144\"/><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"144\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"144\"/><line x1=\"500\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"144\"/><line x1=\"640\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"144\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"238\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"264\"/></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"360\" y=\"39\">First: is each column numerical or categorical?</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"106\">Univariate: one column</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"106\">Bivariate: two columns</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"170\">Numerical</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"170\">Categorical</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"170\">Num – Num</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"170\">Cat – Num</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"170\">Cat – Cat</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"196\">describe()</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"220\">histogram, box</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"196\">value_counts()</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"220\">bar chart</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"196\">corr()</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"220\">scatter plot</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"196\">groupby().mean()</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"220\">grouped box plot</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"196\">pd.crosstab()</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"220\">stacked bar chart</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"291\">Three or more columns: colour by a third column, pair plot, heatmap (3.8), PCA (Unit 5)</text></g>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.5.1</b> The EDA decision map. Start from the type of each column; one column goes left, a pair goes right. Each box gives the pandas call for the numbers and the plot for the picture. The bottom box is where a third variable comes in.</figcaption>\n      </figure>",
 "6": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 392\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The figure drawn by the worked example: a line chart of tea and coffee sales and a bar chart of totals, with Figure and Axes parts labelled\">\n          <defs><marker id=\"m36a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:currentColor\"/></marker></defs>\n          <rect x=\"14\" y=\"40\" width=\"692\" height=\"340\" rx=\"4\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n          <text x=\"14\" y=\"28\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\">Figure: fig, 10 × 4 inches</text>\n          <text x=\"360\" y=\"66\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A Chennai tea stall, Jan–Jun</text>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"241\" y=\"92\">Cups sold per month</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"92\">Six-month total</text></g>\n          <path d=\"M80,100 H390 V320 H80 Z M470,100 H690 V320 H470 Z\" style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.2\"/>\n          <path d=\"M74,320h6 M74,246.7h6 M74,173.3h6 M74,100h6 M106,320v6 M160,320v6 M214,320v6 M268,320v6 M322,320v6 M376,320v6 M464,320h6 M464,271.1h6 M464,222.2h6 M464,173.3h6 M464,124.4h6 M530,320v6 M630,320v6\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.2\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"324\">0</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"251\">60</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"177\">120</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"104\">180</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"324\">0</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"275.1\">200</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"226.2\">400</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"177.3\">600</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"128.4\">800</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"342\">Jan</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"342\">Feb</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"342\">Mar</text><text x=\"268\" y=\"342\">Apr</text><text x=\"322\" y=\"342\">May</text><text x=\"376\" y=\"342\">Jun</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"342\">Tea</text><text x=\"630\" y=\"342\">Coffee</text><text x=\"241\" y=\"366\">Month</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"130.7\">750</text><text x=\"630\" y=\"177.6\">558</text></g>\n          <text transform=\"translate(36,210) rotate(-90)\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cups sold (hundreds)</text>\n          <text transform=\"translate(424,210) rotate(-90)\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cups (hundreds)</text>\n          <polyline points=\"106,173.3 160,155 214,136.7 268,185.6 322,203.9 376,148.9\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M102,173.3a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M156,155a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M210,136.7a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M264,185.6a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M318,203.9a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M372,148.9a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n          <polyline points=\"106,222.2 160,216.1 214,210 268,197.8 322,191.7 376,200.2\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M102,218.2h8v8h-8z M156,212.1h8v8h-8z M210,206h8v8h-8z M264,193.8h8v8h-8z M318,187.7h8v8h-8z M372,196.2h8v8h-8z\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/>\n          <rect x=\"88\" y=\"258\" width=\"92\" height=\"52\" rx=\"4\" style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1\"/>\n          <path d=\"M96,274 H120\" style=\"stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\"/><path d=\"M96,296 H120\" style=\"stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\"><text x=\"128\" y=\"278\">Tea</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"300\">Coffee</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"271\">Summer dip</text></g>\n          <line x1=\"290\" y1=\"258\" x2=\"317\" y2=\"212\" style=\"stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#m36a)\"/>\n          <g style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:1.5\"><rect x=\"495\" y=\"136.7\" width=\"70\" height=\"183.3\"/><rect x=\"595\" y=\"183.6\" width=\"70\" height=\"136.4\"/></g>\n          <g font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\"><text x=\"384\" y=\"118\">Axes: axs[0]</text><text x=\"684\" y=\"118\">Axes: axs[1]</text></g>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.6.1</b> What the worked example's code draws, with its parts named. The dashed outer box is the Figure; each framed plot is an Axes with its own title, ticks and labels. The legend sits in the lower-left corner as asked, the annotation arrow points at May's tea value of 95, and <code>bar_label</code> writes 750 and 558 on the bars.</figcaption>\n      </figure>",
 "7": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 232\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Five small charts from this book's data: bar, pie, histogram, box plot and scatter, each with the question it answers\">\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"30\">Bar</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"30\">Pie</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"30\">Histogram</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"30\">Box</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"30\">Scatter</text></g>\n          <path d=\"M24,44 V160 H140 M300,44 V160 H418 M470,44 V160 M580,44 V160 H702\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.2\"/>\n          <g style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"><rect x=\"30\" y=\"50\" width=\"28\" height=\"110\"/><rect x=\"66\" y=\"116\" width=\"28\" height=\"44\"/><rect x=\"102\" y=\"138\" width=\"28\" height=\"22\"/></g>\n          <path d=\"M220,104 L220,50 A54,54 0 1 0 251.7,147.7 Z\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M220,104 L251.7,147.7 A54,54 0 0 0 271.4,87.3 Z\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M220,104 L271.4,87.3 A54,54 0 0 0 236.7,52.6 Z\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M220,104 L236.7,52.6 A54,54 0 0 0 220,50 Z\" style=\"fill:var(--line2)\"/>\n          <g font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"fill:var(--accent-ink)\"><text x=\"189\" y=\"118\">UPI</text><text x=\"251\" y=\"118\">Card</text></g>\n          <g style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.2\"><rect x=\"304\" y=\"148\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"322\" y=\"124\" width=\"18\" height=\"36\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"88\" width=\"18\" height=\"72\"/><rect x=\"358\" y=\"52\" width=\"18\" height=\"108\"/><rect x=\"376\" y=\"112\" width=\"18\" height=\"48\"/><rect x=\"394\" y=\"136\" width=\"18\" height=\"24\"/></g>\n          <path d=\"M500,149.8 V138.8 M500,110.7 V103.9 M490,149.8 H510 M490,103.9 H510\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n          <rect x=\"482\" y=\"110.7\" width=\"36\" height=\"28.1\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M482,126 H518\" style=\"stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n          <path d=\"M495,57.2a5,5 0 1 0 10,0a5,5 0 1 0 -10,0\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"/>\n          <path d=\"M586,150a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M600.3,137.1a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M628.9,111.4a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M643.1,124.3a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M671.7,85.7a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0 M686,60a4,4 0 1 0 8,0a4,4 0 1 0 -8,0\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"44\" y=\"176\">UPI</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"176\">Card</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"176\">Cash</text><text x=\"304\" y=\"176\">30</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"176\">90</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"176\">runs</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"176\">hours → marks</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"200\">compare</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"218\">categories</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"200\">share of</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"218\">one whole</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"200\">shape of one</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"218\">number column</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"200\">spread and</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"218\">outliers</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"200\">link between</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"218\">two numbers</text></g>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.7.1</b> The five charts, each drawn from this book's own data: payment modes from Chapter 3.5 (bar), the payment shares of worked example 2 below (pie: UPI 60%, Card 20%, Cash 15%, Wallet 5%), the test marks of Chapter 3.1 (histogram), the batter of worked example 1 (box, with the 121 outlier on top) and study hours against marks from Chapter 3.4 (scatter). The grey line under each says the question it answers.</figcaption>\n      </figure>",
 "8": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 362\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Correlation heatmap of hours, attendance, phone and marks for ten students\">\n          <defs><linearGradient id=\"g38a\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" style=\"stop-color:var(--accent);stop-opacity:1\"/><stop offset=\"0.5\" style=\"stop-color:var(--accent);stop-opacity:0\"/><stop offset=\"0.5\" style=\"stop-color:var(--live);stop-opacity:0\"/><stop offset=\"1\" style=\"stop-color:var(--live);stop-opacity:1\"/></linearGradient></defs>\n          <text x=\"400\" y=\"28\" fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">df.corr() as a heatmap: 10 students</text>\n          <g style=\"stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1\">\n            <rect x=\"240\" y=\"48\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:1\"/><rect x=\"310\" y=\"48\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.14\"/><rect x=\"380\" y=\"48\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--live);fill-opacity:.51\"/><rect x=\"450\" y=\"48\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.92\"/>\n            <rect x=\"240\" y=\"118\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.14\"/><rect x=\"310\" y=\"118\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:1\"/><rect x=\"380\" y=\"118\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.04\"/><rect x=\"450\" y=\"118\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.4\"/>\n            <rect x=\"240\" y=\"188\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--live);fill-opacity:.51\"/><rect x=\"310\" y=\"188\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.04\"/><rect x=\"380\" y=\"188\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:1\"/><rect x=\"450\" y=\"188\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--live);fill-opacity:.61\"/>\n            <rect x=\"240\" y=\"258\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.92\"/><rect x=\"310\" y=\"258\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:.4\"/><rect x=\"380\" y=\"258\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--live);fill-opacity:.61\"/><rect x=\"450\" y=\"258\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" style=\"fill:var(--accent);fill-opacity:1\"/>\n          </g>\n          <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"fill:var(--accent-ink)\"><text x=\"275\" y=\"88\">1.00</text><text x=\"485\" y=\"88\">0.92</text><text x=\"345\" y=\"158\">1.00</text><text x=\"415\" y=\"228\">1.00</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"298\">0.92</text><text x=\"485\" y=\"298\">1.00</text></g>\n          <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\"><text x=\"345\" y=\"88\">0.14</text><text x=\"415\" y=\"88\">−0.51</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"158\">0.14</text><text x=\"415\" y=\"158\">0.04</text><text x=\"485\" y=\"158\">0.40</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"228\">−0.51</text><text x=\"345\" y=\"228\">0.04</text><text x=\"485\" y=\"228\">−0.61</text><text x=\"345\" y=\"298\">0.40</text><text x=\"415\" y=\"298\">−0.61</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\"><text x=\"232\" y=\"88\">hours</text><text x=\"232\" y=\"158\">attendance</text><text x=\"232\" y=\"228\">phone</text><text x=\"232\" y=\"298\">marks</text></g>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"275\" y=\"348\">hours</text><text x=\"345\" y=\"348\">attendance</text><text x=\"415\" y=\"348\">phone</text><text x=\"485\" y=\"348\">marks</text></g>\n          <rect x=\"550\" y=\"48\" width=\"20\" height=\"280\" style=\"fill:url(#g38a);stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1\"/>\n          <g fill=\"currentColor\" font-size=\"13\"><text x=\"578\" y=\"58\">+1</text><text x=\"578\" y=\"192\">0</text><text x=\"578\" y=\"328\">−1</text></g>\n        </svg>\n        <figcaption><b>Figure 3.8.1</b> The worked example's correlation matrix as a heatmap. Blue cells are positive, orange negative, and the stronger the colour the larger |r|; the colour bar runs from −1 to +1. The diagonal is always 1, and the two triangles mirror each other. The eye goes straight to hours–marks (0.92) and phone–marks (−0.61).</figcaption>\n      </figure>"
